@Katerina Kelepouri Don't need to read the AI slop above. But this is mostly working. It's part of my attempts to unify and improve the cross messaging experience. Two main things:
- Now even Ship has the notion of unread messages. The styling is not great, but it's there.
- If you read a message in Ship then it's automatically marked for you as read in Peek as well.

@Katerina Kelepouri I did lots of research and created with Claude bunch of refactoring projects in Ship. It will improve the architecture, make it faster and truly use Nostr for everything.

I definitely want to do it before I start Leaf. But I also don't want to block you with cleaning up Ship.

I think you can go ahead and start working on it. I would just advice to steer Claude in a way to focus mainly on the frontend stuff.

@Katerina Kelepouri If you want, you can try it as well now, but it would requires some tedious command line magic on your side.

What it does now is that it allows you to read data from Ship. So you could say something like "Check ticket PEE-1 and implement it".

Alternatively, I will on Friday and over the weekend finish the whole thing including better onboarding to this feature without command lines.
